  2350.0 ? outLamp3=off  "[p.34:] Set the rotary switch dial to 0 and turn power on. Turn the rotary switch clockwise until the pointer knob is pointing at the letter you wish to code. Read the Morse Code representation of the letter starting with output light 3. If the letter you wish to code is in band 1 of the dial plate, read only light 3. / A light on represents a dash. / A light off represents a dot. [p.32:] E · [p.33:] BAND 1 / MORSE CODE: ALPHABETIC DIAL PLATE [errata p.33:] Note to Experiment 19 — always turn the pointer knob clockwise when indicating a letter for coding."
  2350.0 ? outLamp3=off outLamp4=on  "[p.34:] Set the rotary switch dial to 0 and turn power on. Turn the rotary switch clockwise until the pointer knob is pointing at the letter you wish to code. Read the Morse Code representation of the letter starting with output light 3. / If the letter is in band 2, read lights 3 and 4. / A light on represents a dash. / A light off represents a dot. [p.32:] A ·— [p.33:] BAND 2 / MORSE CODE: ALPHABETIC DIAL PLATE [errata p.33:] Note to Experiment 19 — always turn the pointer knob clockwise when indicating a letter for coding."
  2350.0 ? outLamp3=off outLamp4=on outLamp5=on  "[p.34:] Set the rotary switch dial to 0 and turn power on. Turn the rotary switch clockwise until the pointer knob is pointing at the letter you wish to code. Read the Morse Code representation of the letter starting with output light 3. / If the letter is in band 3, read lights 3, 4, 5. / A light on represents a dash. / A light off represents a dot. [p.32:] W ·—— [p.33:] BAND 3 / MORSE CODE: ALPHABETIC DIAL PLATE [errata p.33:] Note to Experiment 19 — always turn the pointer knob clockwise when indicating a letter for coding."
